<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Pawmodoro — iOS entitlements.

  This file is for the iOS build ONLY. It is wired up as
      CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS[sdk=iphoneos*]        = Pawmodoro/iOS/Pawmodoro.entitlements
      CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS[sdk=iphonesimulator*] = Pawmodoro/iOS/Pawmodoro.entitlements
  with the unconditional value left empty, so the macOS build takes
  Pawmodoro/Mac/Pawmodoro.entitlements (App Sandbox, and nothing else) and
  neither platform inherits the other's claims.

  One key, and it is load-bearing:

    - com.apple.security.application-groups = group.com.pawmodoro
      TimerEngine.settingsDidChange() mirrors "widget.buddy" and
      "widget.place" into UserDefaults(suiteName: "group.com.pawmodoro"), and
      PawmodoroWidgets/PawmodoroHomeWidget.swift reads "widget.buddy" back out
      of the same suite. Without this entitlement on BOTH sides, that write
      silently lands in the app's own private container, the widget reads
      nothing, and its `?? "cat"` fallback holds — so everybody's home screen
      draws the cat no matter which buddy they chose. The matching file is
      PawmodoroWidgets/PawmodoroWidgets.entitlements; the two must always
      name the same group.

  Deliberately absent, so nobody adds them back "just in case":

    - No App Sandbox. That is a macOS concept and lives in the Mac file.
    - No network client/server. The app makes zero network calls
      (docs/PRIVACY.md), and on iOS neither entitlement exists anyway.
    - No HealthKit, no CloudKit/iCloud containers, no keychain sharing, no
      associated domains, no push. Nothing in this app talks to any of them.
    - No com.apple.developer.usernotifications.* — plain local notifications
      through UNUserNotificationCenter need no entitlement, and the
      time-sensitive one is a claim this app's notifications do not make.

  Do NOT add com.apple.security.get-task-allow here. Xcode injects it for
  debugging and strips it when archiving; a copy in this file would ship in
  the archive and the upload is rejected.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.pawmodoro</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
